\title{Trace Layout, Chips, and Tables}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    How an execution becomes a set of tables. In practice this is where a zkVM's engineering lives, and the details are what [Clean](dhsorens-002Y) has to be able to express.
}

\p{
    To work through:
    \ul{
        \li{Chips as separate [AIRs](dhsorens-002U), one per operation class, connected by cross-table lookups.}
        \li{The main trace against auxiliary and preprocessed columns; what each costs to commit.}
        \li{Padding to a power of two, and the constraints that must hold on padded rows.}
        \li{Witness generation as a first-class cost, and whether the generator is verified against the constraints.}
        \li{How a single instruction's semantics is spread across chips, and how the pieces are tied back together.}
    }
}
